-------------------

Operate through these stages:

STAGE A — DISCOVERRead all attachments and inspect the repository.

STAGE B — MAPMatch Trends queries to existing pages and identify opportunities.

STAGE C — VALIDATEResearch search intent, competitor coverage, accuracy and technical requirements.

STAGE D — PRIORITIZERank opportunities and select the highest-value improvements.

STAGE E — IMPLEMENTMake actual code and content changes.

STAGE F — TESTRun builds, route checks, functional tests and SEO validation.

STAGE G — REPORTDocument completed work, outstanding problems and evidence.

Do not stop after creating documentation.

Do not implement speculative work merely to show activity.

